/-! # Demo: one Taylor-merged Chebyshev piece of the SN field, alpha = 0.005 (cost measurement)

The piece `[-2349/4096, -1303/4096]` (`-0.573486328`, `-0.318115234`; centre `-0.445801`, radius `0.127686`)
of the refined cover of `q1snFq` against the threshold `q1snT` (piece 18 of the 50-piece greedy cover of
`SN` t1, interval rounded inward to the grid `2^-12`), certified by ONE `chebMergePiece` check:
`Mp = 8`, `Ml = 30`, rounding `2^-100`, `logQ` order 12, `argQ` order 24, Chebyshev data of 72 terms
on the grid `2^-130`.  Data: `qb` (plog sites: `r/|c - e| <= qb <= 1/2`), `(qb, rb)` (poles: `r/|c - p| <= qb`, `|rho| <= rb`)
on the grid `2^-20`, `gamma` = Chebyshev coefficients of the merged polynomial (untrusted).  All 14 merged plog sites and all
171 poles take the Taylor branch.

Conclusion: `fieldTower q1snFq (poleF q1snFq.poles) 0 x <= q1snT` on the piece, the statement of the cells `SnP*`.
-/

